From 5746100bc287a5f82b1312369f37b2c4c391ecd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Thorbj=C3=B8rn=20Ravn=20Andersen?= <tra@ravnand.dk>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:21:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] [Z80] Add
 __builtin_z80_{di,ei,halt,nop,in,out,im0,im1,im2,set_i} clang builtins

C code can now emit DI, EI, HALT, NOP, IN, OUT, IM 0/1/2 and LD I,A without
inline assembly.  Each builtin lowers to the matching llvm.z80.* intrinsic,
which (since the nocallback change) does not cost the calling function its
static frame -- inline assembly does.

The clang plumbing (BuiltinsZ80.td, Z80TargetInfo builtin tables and the
"z80" feature, CodeGen/TargetBuiltins/Z80.cpp, CGBuiltin dispatch) comes from
2883cdd8bb73 (ravn/llvm-z80#42), which is not on main.  Only the clang parts
are taken: the backend part exists on this branch in its own form, and the
shipped <intrinsic.h> is deliberately not restored (the intrinsic_* mapping
belongs in the firmware / z88dk headers).

New compared with that commit: __builtin_z80_in/out and im0/im1.  in, out,
im0/1/2 and set_i are gated on the "z80" feature, so sm83 (no IN/OUT, no
interrupt modes, no I register) gets a clean frontend diagnostic.

Tests: clang/test/CodeGen/z80-builtins.c, z80-builtins-sm83-gate.c.  An
end-to-end C check with -ffreestanding +static-frame gives ld a,64 / ld i,a,
im 2, out (16),a, in a,(17) and a static frame (L_helper.frame, no stack
frame use).  llvm-lit CodeGen/Z80 159/160 (z88dk-runtime.ll fails identically
on the base); 17/17 Z80 clang tests; cargo runtime 462/456/0/6, per-test
results identical to the base.

Rules-checked: lit tests added; both test tiers run before/after; local branch,
not pushed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
